# Laser Puzzle – Console-Based C Project

## Author

Merdan
Computer Engineering Student

---

## Description
This project is a **console-based puzzle game written in C**.  
The objective is to correctly arrange and rotate pipes on a grid so that a laser (flow) starting from a **source** reaches the **target**.

The project focuses on **logic, algorithms, and problem-solving**, not graphics.

---

## Game Logic
- The game uses a **2D grid map**.
- A source cell emits a laser/flow.
- Pipes can be rotated to change the flow direction.
- The flow propagates through connected pipes.
- If the flow reaches the target, the player wins.
- The program checks for valid paths and prevents infinite loops using visited tracking.

---
## Controls

(May vary depending on implementation)

W A S D – Move cursor

R – Rotate pipe

C – Check flow / win condition

Q – Quit

---

